\section{Device parameters}\label{sec:models}

\paragraph{Extraction.} For each device type and length, ngspice sweeps $I_D$--$V_{GS}$ at $|V_{DS}| = 0.9$\,V
($W = 10\,\mu$m). By \eqref{T-eq:sat}, $\sqrt{I_D}$ is a straight line in $V_{GS}$. Its slope gives $\KP$
and its intercept gives $V_{TH}$; the fit uses $\ov = 0.1$--0.3\,V. Next, $\lambda$ is the slope of
$I_D$--$V_{DS}$ at $\ov = 0.2$\,V over $|V_{DS}| = 0.6$--1.2\,V, divided by $I_D$. Table~\ref{tab:par}
lists the results, and Fig.~\ref{fig:gmid} shows the simulated $g_m/I_D$.

