\paragraph{Step 7 -- Buffer} \cite[Eq.~(3)]{rm_jssc}, \cite[Section~2.4]{rm_thesis}. The parasitic pole
at the gate of $M_P$, $p_B = g_{out}/(2\pi C_G)$ (Lemma~\ref{T-lem:sf}; $P_3$ in \cite{rm_jssc}), must lie above
$\fu$. The worst case is full load \cite[Section~2.1]{rm_thesis} with $\RESR\to0$. Proposition~\ref{T-prop:pm}
with a target of $<<60|d>>^\circ$ (the specification, $45^\circ$, plus $15^\circ$ for corners) gives
$\arctan(\fu/p_B) \le 30^\circ - \arctan(\fu/p_{EA})$.
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=0.1ex]
\item \emph{Pass A.} $\fu = <<FA['fu']/1e6|.2f>>$\,MHz and $\arctan(\fu/p_{EA}) = <<FA['phi_ea']|.1f>>^\circ$ leave
<<FA['room_deg']|.1f>>$^\circ$ for the buffer: no bias current reaches the target. The square-law gain, and with it
$\fu$, is too high, which is exactly the optimism the 6\,dB margin of Step~6c anticipated.
\item \emph{Pass B.} At the operating point of v3: $g_{m1}/I_{D1} = <<FB['gmid1']|.1f>>$\,V$^{-1}$,
$\lambda_2 = <<FB['lam2']|.3f>>$, $\lambda_4 = <<FB['lam4']|.3f>>$\,V$^{-1}$, so $\Aea = <<FB['A_ea']|.1f>>$ and $G = <<FB['G']|.1f>>$
(still $<<FB['G_margin']|.2f>>\times G_{min}$). Then $\fu = <<FB['fu']/1e3|.0f>>$\,kHz, $p_{EA} = <<FB['p_ea']/1e6|.2f>>$\,MHz,
$\arctan(\fu/p_{EA}) = <<FB['phi_ea']|.1f>>^\circ$, and the buffer pole must be at least
$p_B = <<FB['pb_min']/1e6|.2f>>$\,MHz: $g_{mB} \ge 2\pi C_G p_B \Ab = <<FB['gmb_min']*1e3|.3f>>$\,mS. With the operating-point
$g_{mB}/I_B = <<FB['gmid_b']|.2f>>$\,V$^{-1}$ this needs $I_B \ge <<FB['I_pole']*1e6|.1f>>\,\mu$A.
\item \emph{Slew current.} For the load release only $I_B$ charges $C_G$ (Remark after
Proposition~\ref{T-prop:budget}). With $1/(2\pi\fu) = <<FB['tau']*1e6|.3f>>\,\mu$s, the budget of Step~5 leaves
$t_{sr} \le <<FB['t_sr_max']*1e6|.2f>>\,\mu$s, so \eqref{T-eq:tsr} needs $I_B \ge <<FB['I_slew']*1e6|.2f>>\,\mu$A. The pole condition is binding.
\end{itemize}
$I_B = <<FB['I_B']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$A (the next multiple of $I_{REF}$; v3 used 30\,$\mu$A). Predictions: $p_B = <<FB['p_b']/1e6|.2f>>$\,MHz,
PM $= <<FB['PM_esr0']|.1f>>^\circ$ ($\RESR = 0$) and $<<FB['PM_esr']|.1f>>^\circ$ ($\RESR = 10$\,m$\Omega$), $t_{sr} = <<FB['t_sr']*1e6|.2f>>\,\mu$s. The
load-step excursion by \eqref{T-eq:budget} is at most <<FB['dv_tr_thesis']*1e3|.0f>>\,mV with the conservative $t_{loop} = 1/\fu$
of \cite{rm_thesis}, or <<FB['dv_tr_tau']*1e3|.1f>>\,mV with $t_{loop} = 1/(2\pi\fu)$, both within 50\,mV. $M_{BS}$ mirrors $I_{REF}$
($W_{BS} = <<Z4['WBS']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$m) and $M_B$ is sized by \eqref{T-eq:sat} at $V_{OV,B}$: $W_B = <<Z4['WB']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$m, $L_B = <<Z4['LB']*1e6|.1f>>\,\mu$m.

\paragraph{Step 8 -- Quiescent current and current efficiency} \cite[Eq.~(1)]{rm_jssc}.
$I_Q = I_{REF} + 2I_{D1} + I_B + I_R = <<F['s8']['Iq']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$A (v3: <<F['s8']['Iq_v3']*1e6|.0f>>\,$\mu$A), within the
$<<SP['IQ_MAX']*1e6|.0f>>\,\mu$A limit. The current efficiency $\IL/(\IL+I_Q)$ is <<F['s8']['eff_min']*100|.0f>>\,\% at
<<SP['IL_MIN']*1e3|.1f>>\,mA and <<F['s8']['eff_max']*100|.2f>>\,\% at <<SP['IL_MAX']*1e3|.0f>>\,mA. Pass~B removes the
<<(F['s8']['Iq_v3']-F['s8']['Iq'])*1e6|.0f>>\,$\mu$A by which the buffer of v3 was over-biased, which is the aim of the procedure:
the least quiescent current that the stability and transient requirements allow \cite{rm_jssc}.

