columns: $\VIN\in\{1.8,1.9\}$\,V, $T\in\{0,27,85\}\,^\circ$C, both load ends).
Values that miss the specification are marked with $\times$.}
\label{tab:iter}
\begin{tabular}{lcccc}
\toprule
& v1 & v2 & v3 & v4 (final)\\
\midrule
$L_{12}$ / $L_{34}$ ($\mu$m), $V_{OV,B}$ (V) & 1 / 1, 0.15 & 2 / 2, 0.15 & 1 / 3, <<V3['vov_b']|.2f>> & 1 / 3, <<FB['vov_b']|.2f>>\\
Buffer current $I_B$ ($\mu$A) & 30 & 30 & 30 & <<FB['I_B']*1e6|.0f>>\\
Simulated $\Aea$ at full load & <<D1['heavy']['A_ea']|.0f>> & <<D2['heavy']['A_ea']|.0f>> & <<D3['heavy']['A_ea']|.0f>> & <<D4['heavy']['A_ea']|.0f>>\\
PSRR at 1\,kHz, 50\,mA (dB) & <<S1['psrr']['50mA']['1kHz']|.1f>> $\times$ & <<S2['psrr']['50mA']['1kHz']|.1f>> & <<S3['psrr']['50mA']['1kHz']|.1f>> & <<S4['psrr']['50mA']['1kHz']|.1f>>\\
Line regulation, worst (mV/V) & <<max(S1['linereg']['0.1mA']['slope'],S1['linereg']['50mA']['slope'])*1e3|.1f>> $\times$ & <<max(S2['linereg']['0.1mA']['slope'],S2['linereg']['50mA']['slope'])*1e3|.1f>> & <<max(S3['linereg']['0.1mA']['slope'],S3['linereg']['50mA']['slope'])*1e3|.1f>> & <<max(S4['linereg']['0.1mA']['slope'],S4['linereg']['50mA']['slope'])*1e3|.1f>>\\
PM at 50\,mA (deg) & <<S1['loop']['50mA']['PM']|.1f>> & <<S2['loop']['50mA']['PM']|.1f>> & <<S3['loop']['50mA']['PM']|.1f>> & <<S4['loop']['50mA']['PM']|.1f>>\\
PM, $\RESR = 0$, worst corner (deg) & -- & <<C2['pm_esr0_min']|.1f>> $\times$ & <<C3['pm_esr0_min']|.1f>> & <<C4['pm_esr0_min']|.1f>>\\
PSRR at 1\,kHz, worst corner (dB) & -- & <<C2['psrr_nom_min']|.1f>> $\times$ & <<C3['psrr_nom_min']|.1f>> & <<C4['psrr_nom_min']|.1f>>\\
$I_Q$ ($\mu$A) & <<S1['iq']['at_1p8']*1e6|.1f>> & <<S2['iq']['at_1p8']*1e6|.1f>> & <<S3['iq']['at_1p8']*1e6|.1f>> & <<S4['iq']['at_1p8']*1e6|.1f>>\\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\begin{itemize}[itemsep=0.2ex]
\item \textbf{v1} ($L = 1\,\mu$m everywhere) is stable, with a large margin, but its EA gain is only
<<D1['heavy']['A_ea']|.0f>> against <<V1['A_ea']|.0f>> by the square law. As a result, PSRR and line regulation miss. This
is the gain optimism that the 6\,dB margin of Step~6c now covers.
\item \textbf{v2} doubles $L$ for $M_1$--$M_4$. The gain rises, but by Proposition~\ref{T-prop:pea} $p_{EA}$
falls (it scales as $\lambda/L$), and the phase margin with $\RESR = 0$ drops to
<<C2['pm_esr0_min']|.1f>>$^\circ$ at $\VIN = 1.9$\,V, 85\,$^\circ$C. At light load and $\VIN = 1.9$\,V, $\VEA$
also rises to within <<(SP['VREF']+P['p_L1.00']['VTH']) - O2['vinmax_light']['v(ea)']|.2f>>\,V of the bound $\VREF+|V_{TH,p}|$ of
Proposition~\ref{T-prop:window}. $M_2$ then nears triode and the PSRR falls to <<C2['psrr_nom_min']|.1f>>\,dB.
This is the reason for the shortest-$L_{12}$ rule of Step~6c.
\item \textbf{v3} lengthens only the mirror ($L_{34} = 3\,\mu$m), because the simulated operating point
shows that $g_{ds4}$, not $g_{ds2}$, dominates the EA output conductance, and moves $V_{OV,B}$ to the centre of
the window \eqref{T-eq:window}. Its buffer current, 30\,$\mu$A, was a budget choice. v3 meets every specification.
\item \textbf{v4} is the outcome of the procedure of Section~\ref{sec:hand}: Step~6c reproduces the lengths of
v3, and Pass~B of Step~7 sets the buffer current from the pole and slew conditions, <<FB['I_B']*1e6|.0f>>\,$\mu$A. The
quiescent current falls by <<(S3['iq']['at_1p8']-S4['iq']['at_1p8'])*1e6|.1f>>\,$\mu$A; the phase margin at full load falls by
<<S3['loop']['50mA']['PM']-S4['loop']['50mA']['PM']|.1f>>$^\circ$ and stays above the 60$^\circ$ target with $\RESR = 0$ at the nominal point.
\end{itemize}

